From: Ville Vesilehto <ville@vesilehto.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: detect Apple Silicon as the Arm processor family

macOS reports CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR as "arm64", which family.cmake
matches neither as "arm" nor as "aarch64", so PROCESSOR_FAMILY becomes
"Other" and isa.cmake never runs its ARM checks. HAVE_ARM_NEON is then
left undefined and every hash builds without NEON: XXH3 falls back to
its scalar path and gxhash to its portable one, which makes any speed
comparison on Apple Silicon unfair to SIMD hashes.

Match "arm64" as well.

diff --git a/platform/family.cmake b/platform/family.cmake
index 3ae67389..27abb8e7 100644
--- a/platform/family.cmake
+++ b/platform/family.cmake
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ if ((CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "x86_64")
     OR (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "x86"))
   set(PROCESSOR_FAMILY "x86")
 elseif ((CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "arm")
+    OR (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "arm64") # apple silicon
     OR (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR STREQUAL "aarch64"))
   set(PROCESSOR_FAMILY "Arm")
 else ()
